      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the case of a 58-year-old woman who underwent outpatient coronary angiography with 5F catheters for atypical chest pain. Superselective angiography of a right superior septal artery mimicked a coronary arteriovenous fistula. Appropriate placement of the catheter in the ostium of the right coronary artery excluded the suspected anomaly."},
